error[NK1131]: You can't give away `h.name` here: `h` is only borrowed.
   --> tests/a_pub_function_refuses_a_borrowed_field_in_a_mixed_arm.nika:10:52
    |
 10 | pub fn by_if(h: ref H, c: bool) -> String { if c { h.name } else { own(h.name) } }
    |                                                    ^^^^^^
    |
    = note: `h` belongs to whoever lent it (a parameter without `keep`, a `for` over a list, a `let` over a place), and `h.name` is a `String`. Giving it away would take a piece out of something this function doesn't own.
    = help: Write `h.name.clone()` for a copy. A result that is a view of a parameter on every way out is handed back as it is, with no mark.
